const notes = "<p>Miami Beach requires an approved tree work permit to remove or relocate a tree or palm, with a short list of exceptions, and expects removals to be justified and trees replaced or relocated. Applicants usually provide a tree survey, a disposition and an arborist report by an ISA or ASCA certified arborist.</p><p>Trees in the swale are maintained by the adjacent owner, but removing one still needs a permit from the city's urban forestry division. Condominium buildings also need association approval.</p>";

